# Every variable the backend reads: what it is and where to get it. Names only, never values.
# Copy to backend/.env (gitignored) for local dev and fill in what you need. On Fly the same
# names are set as secrets by ob1-can-obi. Everything is optional: without a group, the
# feature it enables is skipped and the UI says why.

# --- GitHub: Build locks commits and checks guardrails; the Planner opens PRs --------------
# Any token that can read the MaC-aroni repos. Easiest: `gh auth token` after `gh auth login`.
# Without it Builds still work on the public repos but hit GitHub's anonymous rate limit.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- LLM: the Planner, the knowledge-graph ingest, guide/code writers, the design page -----
# For the Nemotron track use NVIDIA NIM: key from https://build.nvidia.com (open a model,
# "Get API Key" / "View Code"). Then MAC_LLM_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1 and
# MAC_LLM_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b (the defaults; the 120B 404s on NIM chat). Any OpenAI-compatible API
# works for testing (set all three). NVIDIA_API_KEY is accepted as an alias for the key.
# MAC_LLM_API_KEY=
# MAC_LLM_BASE_URL=
# MAC_LLM_MODEL=
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# --- Atlassian: MaC raises the approval tickets in Jira and writes pages in Confluence -----
# One site for both. Site URL from the Atlassian admin (looks like https://<site>.atlassian.net).
# Token: https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens, created by the account
# whose email you put in ATLASSIAN_EMAIL. Space key is the Confluence space the team made
# (CLAIMS); the Jira project key defaults to MAC.
# ATLASSIAN_SITE=
# ATLASSIAN_EMAIL=
# ATLASSIAN_API_TOKEN=
# CONFLUENCE_SPACE_KEY=
# JIRA_PROJECT=
# JIRA_ISSUE_TYPE=
# MAC_JIRA_ASSIGNEES=

# --- AWS: the runner's credentials for Rehearse and Deploy (docs/cloud-setup.md) ----------
# The `mac-runner` IAM user's access key, created by whoever set up the AWS account (Zafeer);
# it arrives as a CSV or terminal output, never through chat. The state bucket is
# mac-terraform-state-<account-id> in us-east-1. Use AWS_PROFILE instead of the key pair if
# you keep the key in ~/.aws/credentials.
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_PROFILE=
# MAC_TF_STATE_BUCKET=
# MAC_TF_STATE_REGION=

# --- Where things live (defaults are fine locally) ---------------------------------------
# MAC_DATA_DIR: run history, tickets, graph.json and generated plans (default .mac/ at the repo
# root; /data on Fly). MAC_KNOWLEDGE_DIR: the Confluence drafts the agents read (default
# demo-data/confluence).
# The migrations the console shows are mirrored from MAC_MIGRATIONS_REPO (default
# MaC-aroni/mac-migrations, branch MAC_MIGRATIONS_BRANCH=main: its migrations/*/migration.yaml)
# into MAC_DATA_DIR/migrations every MAC_MIGRATIONS_SYNC_SECONDS (default 60; 0 = off), with the
# bundled examples/ as backup. The Planner's PRs go to the same repo. Set MAC_MIGRATIONS_DIR to
# read one folder instead and mirror nothing.
# MAC_DATA_DIR=
# MAC_KNOWLEDGE_DIR=
# MAC_MIGRATIONS_REPO=
# MAC_MIGRATIONS_BRANCH=
# MAC_MIGRATIONS_SYNC_SECONDS=
# MAC_MIGRATIONS_DIR=

# The knowledge base the AI help cites (default: demo-data/confluence in the repo)
# MAC_KNOWLEDGE_DIR=

# Approvals follow Jira on their own: the server asks Jira every N seconds (default 30; 0 = off),
# and Jira can push changes to POST /api/mac/jira/webhook?token=<secret> (docs/cloud-setup.md).
# MAC_APPROVAL_POLL_SECONDS=30
# MAC_JIRA_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Sign in with GitHub on the live console (only where APP_ENV=production) ---------------
# A GitHub OAuth app in the MaC-aroni org (Settings → Developer settings → OAuth Apps) with
# callback https://deployed-on-a-prayer.fly.dev/api/auth/callback. Not needed locally.
# GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# MAC_GITHUB_REPO=
